67
00:03:08,733 --> 00:03:09,833
You wanted them to find you?

68
00:03:09,833 --> 00:03:11,700
No. I couldn't stop panting.

69
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:12,667
Oh, right.

70
00:03:12,667 --> 00:03:14,900
There was a well. A really deep well.

71
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:20,233
We dropped stones and timed the splash
to work out how deep it was.

72
00:03:20,233 --> 00:03:22,933
It felt like something mysterious was down there.

73
00:03:22,933 --> 00:03:23,733
Me too.

74
00:03:23,733 --> 00:03:24,667
Like an underground cave.

75
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:25,300
When I was little...

76
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:26,633
This is a little shop.

77
00:03:26,633 --> 00:03:29,367
I used to play there all the time.

78
00:03:29,367 --> 00:03:30,900
Nobody at home looked after me.

79
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:33,300
The old lady there was so kind.

80
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:34,900
She gave me snacks and toys.

81
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:35,833
And later...

82
00:03:36,067 --> 00:03:37,800
I lived here in primary school.

83
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:39,567
Seven or eight years later,

84
00:03:39,567 --> 00:03:41,567
